===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|vert}}, borrowed from {{der|en|fro|vert}}, from {{der|en|VL.|virdis}}, syncopated from Classical {{der|en|la|viridis}}. {{doublet|en|virid}}, which was borrowed directly from Latin.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|tincture}} A [[green]] colour, now only in heraldry; represented in engraving by [[diagonal]] parallel lines 45 degrees [[counter-clockwise]].
#: {{color panel|008000}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} Green undergrowth or other vegetation growing in a forest, as a potential cover for [[deer]].
# {{lb|en|archaic}} The right to fell [[trees]] or cut shrubs in a forest.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1819|author=Walter Scott|title=Ivanhoe|passage=“I understand thee,” said the King, “and the Holy Clerk shall have a grant of '''vert''' and venison in my woods of Warncliffe.”}}

